<h1>AbeGaming</h1>

<p>A few helper tools for my gaming friends. See the <a href="about">About page</a> for more information and useful links.
<i>Probably the most important feature is the calculation of expected statistics for battle outcomes: they could help planning your next move.</i>
</p>

<h2>Available Tools</h2>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> <a href="contact">feedback</a> is very welcome!</p>
<ul>
    <li><a href="ftpbattle">For The People - Battle Calculator</a>:
        Single result and/or stats for the legendary "For The People" boardgame by
        <a href="https://www.e-markherman.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Mark Herman</a>
        and <a href="https://www.gmtgames.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GMT Games</a>.<br />
        <i>Roll the dice to get a single result for a given battle,
        or calculate the probabilities of victory, distribution of casualties,
        and other relevant expected values for a given battle setup.</i>        
    </li>
    <li><a href="pogbattle">Paths of Glory - Battle Calculator</a>:
        Same tool for the just-as-legendary "Paths of Glory" boardgame by Ted Raicer and
        <a href="https://www.gmtgames.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GMT Games</a>.
    </li>
    <li>The Napoleonic Wars <strong>BETA</strong> - three calculators for "The Napoleonic Wars" by Mark McLaughlin and
        <a href="https://www.gmtgames.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GMT Games</a>,
        each with probabilities of outcomes and a single-roll result:
        <ul>
            <li><a href="tnwbattle">Land Battle Calculator</a>:
                victory, second Round, rout, Overrun and loss probabilities.
            </li>
            <li><a href="tnwnaval">Naval Battle Calculator</a>:
                similar but for naval battles,both at sea or entering an enemy Port.
            </li>
            <li><a href="tnwsiege">Siege Calculator</a>:
                ditto for Sieges.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<div class="alert alert-info mt-4">
    <strong>📱 Tip:</strong> You can <a href="install">install this as an app</a> on your phone or desktop for offline access.
</div>

